so it's a beautiful day and I have the  great privilege of not being stuck in an  office or working otherwise in a stuffy  cubicle somewhere instead I'm here in  waffled Park Ealing enjoying the Sun  trying not to get pooed on by birds I  did already get peed on by a bird I am  actually working I'm collecting b-roll  for a video I'm making and I thought  this to be a good opportunity to talk  about a topic I find very interesting  called lifestyle design which is all  about you know being able to work in the  environment that you enjoy and making  your work fits around your lifestyles  instead of the other way around so let's  talk about that shall we  so what is lifestyle design well I  basically literally just told you if you  were listening you would know I said it  was fitting your work around your  lifestyle instead of your lifestyle  around your work so typically we try and  find a job we feel very privileged to  have found whatever job we were  fortunate to get and then we move to  whatever location we need to move to in  order to do that job or we just fit our  lifestyle around that routine there's a  couple sort of really getting it on over  there this a little bit distracting  sorry  so we fit our routine basically around  our work and that means often not only  going to work boss of commuting to and  from work and then having only a few  hours in the evening in which to spend  our free time and feeling naked so the  alternative to this is to flip the idea  on its head instead you think what does  the lifestyle I want and what's the job  that will support that lifestyle so to a  lot of people this means becoming a  digital nomad and a digital nomad is  someone who travels the world was  working on the laptop they work online  and this enables them to work them  anywhere as long as they have a plug and  Wi-Fi which most places in the world  these days do so they can travel to  across Europe across America or wherever  sitting cafes during the day typing away  and then in evenings go and explore or  vice versa and to them that's like the  pinnacle of what they want to do at that  time and they believe they've achieved  freedom etc from that and to a lot of  people the idea of being a digital nomad  and lifestyle design they're synonymous  however if you only focus on being a  digital nomad you're kind of missing the  point because lifestyle design is about  building the lifestyle you want and that  might not mean travelling all the time  for me traveling all the time would be a  little bit much I would miss my creature  comforts like cups of tea and comics on  a Wednesday and I also have a wife and  I'd probably miss her an awful lot and  so in general it doesn't really suit me  to be constantly traveling around the  globe I like to travel a little bit more  than your average and fortunately my job  affords me that but I also just like to  have a more laid-back lifestyle instead  of commuting to work like still work out  in the morning I like to sit in coffee  shops around London or visit um nice  locations and I like the privilege to  come and be able to work somewhere like  this and do things that I really enjoy  like working on projects like this video  other videos my website my apps and I  get a lot more reward from that so I  thought what's the lifestyle I want  and that is the lifestyle of the pioneer  and then I thought how do I make this  happen instead of thinking I'm gonna do  this job right now how do I make my life  work around that and working online  isn't the only way to do this in fact  the only way anything you need to do is  to realize that there are lots of ways  to achieve your goals and you need to  know what your goals are so a lot of  people they work towards this invisible  end point where they're going to retire  and have this amazing life but do you  really want to wait until you retired to  actually start living life I say no and  I think so should you instead it makes  more sense to try and live the life you  want now and I think actually for most  of us we have the means to have the  lifestyle that we want already within  our grasp so for instance if you want to  travel more what I do is I got on cheap  holidays easy easy jet and I'm fortunate  to have a friend pilot meaning I can get  extra for cheap flights but to be honest  a flight to Europe for me cost the same  as visiting my home in Bournemouth so  it's negligible the fact that I can work  online means that I can work as I go I  means I have to take time off work it  also means that when I want to take time  off work or after asking on submission  and I can go away for three or four days  at time stay with a friend maybe or  visit somewhere stay in an air B&amp;B very  cheaply there's no reason for me not to  travel as much as I like and you can  probably do the same thing your work  might be more flexible than you realize  if you ask about taking a little bit of  time off or perhaps working from home  then taking your laptop with you to  another country they're not going to  know so yeah you can travel more and  have what you want or perhaps what you  want is a massive house well that's fine  all you have to do is put your resources  that you already have into that massive  house so instead of trying to earn more  and more money instead to try and  increase your wealth by changing the way  you spend your money because here's the  other tip your wealth is not directly  tied to your income for starters you can  have more than one income I make money  from my writing from videos from my  website from apps but if you've got a  full time job you can also decide to cut  people's hair or rent out a room on  Airbnb or to students you know there's  this whole sharing economy thing you  could decide to sell crafts on eBay what  I'm saying is there's no reason that you  have to think I have to get a promotion  after work harder to get more money  that's actually often a lot of other  ways to get money and sometimes it just  means spending less money on things you  don't really need like I know that I buy  computer games sometimes before I finish  playing the other game I just bought  Bastion and I bought transistor because  those games were on  she'll offer on Steam but I haven't  finished playing Fury yet so why did I  do that I don't know but if you stopped  doing that sort of thing and you stopped  spending money in the places you don't  need it you'll have more to spend money  on things you want so again it's just  know your goal and knowing what it is  you want to achieve and then once you do  that you might realize that actually the  easiest way for you to get what you want  the lifestyle you want even if that's  just spending more time with your family  might be to work as a dustbin collector  because then you're finished early in  the day actually surprisingly well-paid  and it's a stable income and maybe you  don't need that much more money you  realize to do the things you want to do  so instead of working harder and harder  and thinking the anywhere can spend more  time with my family is conversely to  work harder and longer hours you just  think actually what is the easiest way  to get to where I want to go instead of  shooting for the stars because you never  know what's around the corner instead of  aiming for the light at the end of the  tunnel make it happen now and work out  what the best way to make that happen is  another tip is that you can be whatever  you want to be without means to sound  too much like a cheesy car bumper  sticker you can be whatever you want to  be right now it's only being hard no  that's wrong you can be whatever you  want to be right now it's only been good  that's the hard bit so for instance if  you want to be a famous music artist  that's hard but if you wanna be a music  artist that's easy all you have to do is  start recording music in your spare time  so for instance my sister she is an  artist she did an art degree and instead  of focusing on becoming an artist  because she realized that the path of an  artist is a hard one she's actually now  a saleswoman and she works on her art in  her spare time and she gets just as much  pleasure out of that that that she would  from doing it as her main job so she can  earn her money come home and then work  on her projects in a kind of more  relaxed atmosphere and she just sell  them and she doesn't make some money on  the side she's doing living a dream but  she's also doing a job the two things  don't need to be Wed to one another  another way if you wanted to become a  famous music artist perhaps instead of  working really hard and trying to get  noticed by a record label create your  own YouTube channel and start sharing  music on there as soon as you start  doing that playing you're on track to  being the thing you want to be and even  if you never quite accomplished it  you'll still get that sense of reward in  the sense of progress that comes just  from doing it because I get so much  reward out doing this channel even  though this video will probably get a  hundred views I don't care I love doing  it and the biennium and you know and  I don't know what that means I don't why  I did in American accent but the point  is I'm having fun and it doesn't  necessarily have to be tied to your  career the way I've achieved the  lifestyle I want which is to wake up a  bit later go to the gym or work out from  home work in a coffee shop and then work  on my own projects until my wife gets  home and then have a chill evening  whoever achieved that is to work online  and that was also what gives me the  freedom to travel a bit more etc but  that doesn't have to be your path if you  are interested in working online now  we'll be making more videos on this I'm  personally a writer a freelance writer  and I've also extended into a couple of  other areas like videos and also app  creation of course and I've made a video  on app creation and I'll talk a bit  about how I work as a writer it's  actually very easy I posted three  adverts and it's given me work for seven  years so I'll tell you how I did that  and you can do the same thing in a  future video but for now the lifestyle  design instead of thinking about what's  my job and how to make my life work  around it think about what's the  lifestyle I want and what job is the  best way to get there and it might  surprise you what the answer is  think of it outside the box so yes a  little bit of ramble but I hope you  found it interesting and useful if you  want more about lifestyle design I  highly recommend the book the 4-hour  workweek by Tim Ferriss he pretty much  coined the phrase and yeah good luck  with it if you enjoyed this video please  like share and subscribe and I'll see  you for the next one which could be  about me kopecks fitness productivity  technology who knows but it's always  about action self-development and yeah  see you then and thanks very much for  watching bye for now
 

